# AI / Vercel AI SDK Rules

## Core Rule
**Always use Vercel AI SDK — never call OpenAI REST API directly.**

```typescript
// ✅ Correct
import { generateText } from "ai"
import { openai } from "@ai-sdk/openai"

// ❌ Never do this
import OpenAI from "openai"
const client = new OpenAI()
```

## Syllabus Generation (Structured Output)

Use `generateObject` with Zod schema for structured JSON.

```typescript
import { generateObject } from "ai"
import { openai } from "@ai-sdk/openai"
import { z } from "zod"

const SyllabusSchema = z.object({
  classes: z.array(z.object({
    order_index: z.number(),
    title: z.string(),
    topics: z.array(z.string()).min(5).max(8),
    duration_minutes: z.literal(80),
  }))
})

const { object } = await generateObject({
  model: openai("gpt-4o"),
  schema: SyllabusSchema,
  prompt: `Break down "${subjectName}" into an 80-min-per-class syllabus.
Each class must have 5-8 topics, ordered from foundational to advanced.`,
})
```

## Homework Generation (Markdown Output)

Use `generateText` for free-form markdown.

```typescript
import { generateText } from "ai"
import { openai } from "@ai-sdk/openai"

const { text } = await generateText({
  model: openai("gpt-4o"),
  prompt: `
Context: You are an expert educational designer building a curriculum for a highly motivated student.
The student has just completed a 1-hour 20-minute class on "${classTitle}".
Topics covered: ${topics.join(", ")}.

Task: Design a challenging homework assignment that requires critical thinking,
problem-solving, and synthesis of the material — not memorization.

Constraints:
- ~45 minutes to complete
- Include a real-world scenario or case study
- No multiple-choice or definition questions
- Output in strict Markdown format

Ethics: Engaging, inclusive, and free of bias.
  `.trim(),
})
```

## Model Selection
- Default: `openai("gpt-4o")` for all generation
- Do not hardcode model strings elsewhere — reference from a single config if needed

## WebRTC / OpenAI Realtime API
- Used exclusively on the Active Class page (`/classroom/[subjectId]/[classId]`)
- Implement as a Client Component with `"use client"`
- WebRTC setup lives in `lib/realtime/` — not inlined in the page component
- MVP: voice playback only — no recording, no speed control

## What to Avoid
- Calling OpenAI SDK directly (use Vercel AI SDK wrappers)
- Putting raw prompt strings in components — keep them in API routes or `lib/ai/`
- Forgetting to handle generation errors (network failures, content policy blocks)
- Using `streamText` when the full response is needed before DB write (use `generateText`)
